      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS exceeds analyst expectations while revenues lag behind",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: ₹4.43 loss per share (down from ₹65.01 profit in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹3.41t (down 22% from FY 2025). Net loss: ₹16.3b (down 107% from profit in FY 2025). Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.5%. Earnings per share (EPS) exceeded analyst estimates. Revenue is forecast to grow 12% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 7.9% growth forecast for the Auto industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 22% per year but the company’s share price has only fallen by 12% per year, which means it has not declined as severely as earnings.",
